  "body": "Stacked on #161 (issue/110-pause-home) → #147 (issue/112-coolant). Retarget each to main before its parent merges.\n\n## What changed\n\nA post \"Output\" option: **One program** (the default; byte-identical output, goldens unchanged) or **One file per operation**.\n\n- Per-op files are named `<program>_<nn>_<op>.<ext>`. The program part is the project file name, or `program` if unsaved. `nn` is in program order with at least two digits. The op part keeps letters, digits, `-` and `_`, up to 48 characters. The extension comes from the post script.\n- Each file is the op posted on its own through the same post: header and units, its own tool change, safe start (G90, the work offset, G40/G49/G80, that op's spindle and coolant) and its own end (M9, M5, home, M30). There's no extra retract ahead of the op's own clearance move, the same as op 1 in the combined program (RECOMMENDED.md).\n- Suppressed ops get no file. Fanuc, Mazak and Fanuc Lathe count O0001, O0002…; Haas, Siemens and Heidenhain write no O-word, as today.\n- A refusal anywhere writes nothing: the job checks run once, and every op's own post must come back with no warnings. Files go to a temp folder and are renamed into place, and a failed rename rolls back the files already moved.\n- `PostOptions.per_op`, set via the existing undoable `SetPostOptions`. It's saved as `per_op_files` only when it's on.\n- UI: with per-op chosen, Post asks for a folder, and the NC viewer shows the first file.\n- New `posting_per_op.rs` and `state_per_op.rs`.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `per_op_files` (9):\n  - `a_two_op_job_writes_two_standalone_programs`\n  - `a_suppressed_op_writes_no_file`\n  - `file_names_are_sanitised`\n  - `a_numbering_dialect_counts_its_o_word_per_file`\n  - `the_lathe_post_numbers_its_programs_the_same_way`\n  - `a_refusal_in_op_two_writes_nothing`\n  - `the_output_option_undoes_and_redoes`\n  - `the_output_option_round_trips_and_old_files_load_one_program`\n  - `the_combined_program_still_numbers_o0001_and_is_unchanged_by_the_split`\n- ui: `output_per_op_commits_undoes_and_posts_into_a_folder`\n- Green: after_op, coolant, fanuc_post, posting, conformance, all camcraft-post tests; UI snapshots unchanged. Clippy on post, app and ui is clean.\n\nChangelog: Post \"Output\" option: one combined program (default) or one standalone NC file per operation (<program>_<nn>_<op>.nc, own tool change, safe start and end, counted O-numbers); a refusal in any op writes nothing\n\nFixes #111\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
